Sure! Here’s how you can invoke the `train_random_forest_classifier` function twice—once for each dataset with the specified parameters:

```json
[
  {
    "function": "train_random_forest_classifier",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset": "dataset1",
      "max_depth": 10,
      "n_estimators": 100
    }
  },
  {
    "function": "train_random_forest_classifier",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset": "dataset2",
      "max_depth": 20,
      "n_estimators": 200
    }
  }
]
```

This will train a Random Forest on `dataset1` with a maximum depth of 10 and 100 trees, and then train another Random Forest on `dataset2` with a maximum depth of 20 and 200 trees.
